WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.045 --> 00:00:03.668
(audience cheers)

00:00:03.668 --> 00:00:05.550
- I just learned this.
I love this about you.

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:07.064
Your middle name is Jazz.

00:00:07.064 --> 00:00:08.070
- Yeah.

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:10.770
- Is one of your parents huge into jazz?

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:14.430
- I literally just texted
my dad saying, "Why Jazz?"

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:17.580
And he replied, "Me like Daisy Jazz."

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.410
- Me Like Daisy Jazz.
- That's it.

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:20.550
- Caveman.
- Yeah.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:22.145
- Me like Daisy Jazz.

00:00:22.145 --> 00:00:23.093
- Texting is so caveman.

00:00:23.093 --> 00:00:25.110
- I know, but it's such a rad middle name.

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:25.943
I've never heard that.

00:00:25.943 --> 00:00:28.110
- Yeah, my middle sister is Kika-Rose.

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:30.240
So he chose the Kika,
my mom chose the Rose.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.190
And then my eldest is Poppy Sophia.

00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:34.042
- Oh, all flowers in there.
- Yeah.

00:00:34.042 --> 00:00:35.163
- I like it. I'm obsessed

00:00:35.163 --> 00:00:35.996
with flowers.
- Also, I'm shook

00:00:35.996 --> 00:00:36.829
from that performance.

00:00:36.829 --> 00:00:38.270
- Oh, you're so...
(audience applauds)

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:39.103
Thank you.

00:00:40.018 --> 00:00:41.042
(Daisy claps)
(audience cheers)

00:00:41.042 --> 00:00:42.352
Do you...?

00:00:42.352 --> 00:00:43.890
I mean, I bet you do.

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:45.390
The only way that's relatable is

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:48.420
I never sing something
generally the same twice.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:50.310
Especially when it comes to blues music.

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:51.510
Are you like that in like acting like

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:53.370
when you do different scenes constantly,

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:55.410
are they always slightly different?

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:58.440
- Yes, I think in the world of,

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:02.910
but also I think now
having produced two films.

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:05.370
But my film, which is a different film

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:07.710
to the one I'm here to talk
about. But it's called "Magpie."

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:09.420
It's very helpful in the edit too,

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:10.920
to have slightly different things.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.030
Because sometimes you're like, "Oh, yeah.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:13.290
Maybe that works a little better

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:15.120
in the context of film."
- In how it edits in.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:17.130
Yeah, same thing with singing, yeah.

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:18.570
Do you love producing? 'Cause yeah,

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:20.430
now you're producing as well.

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:23.010
- Yeah, my first love is acting.

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:26.370
But it's nice to be like,
"Let's get this done."

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:28.140
- Let's get it in, get in there.

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:29.010
Well 'cause not everybody...

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:30.900
I don't like producing even in music.

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:33.957
I like doing what I do and then
everybody else will produce.

00:01:33.957 --> 00:01:36.420
But I have a lot of music friends that...

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:37.530
Musicians who do everything,

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.910
and they're really gifted at that.

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:40.440
That's not a talent that everybody has.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:42.000
- I mean, I don't do everything.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.320
- No, I just mean as an actor though,

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:45.837
and also producing, maybe
directing, like a people person.

00:01:45.837 --> 00:01:47.610
There are certain people that
really have that capability.

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:48.540
- I mean, there are other people

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:50.700
who are so much better
at all of the stuff.

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:52.800
But with the film I made with my husband,

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.210
he called me the engine.

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:55.710
'Cause I was like, "We are gonna do this

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:56.700
and this is how we're gonna do it."

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:58.673
- Thomas, the little engine.
- Oh, Thomas.

00:01:58.673 --> 00:02:00.570
- Thomas, the little engine that could.

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:01.719
I like it, I like it.

00:02:01.719 --> 00:02:03.580
I have kids.
- Amazing.

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:05.610
- Wait, are you good
at keeping resolutions?

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:07.140
We're still early in the year.

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:09.210
Are you good at making
them and keeping them?

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:11.130
I'm not.
- Right.

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:13.800
- Yeah, I don't even know why I make 'em.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.420
I'm never gonna learn Spanish fully.

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:16.253
It's just never gonna happen.

00:02:16.253 --> 00:02:17.880
(audience laughs)
Never gonna happen.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:18.870
I just need to accept it.

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:20.580
- Mm.
- I can get by.

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:21.600
- That's good though.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.401
- Is it? It's settling.

00:02:23.401 --> 00:02:24.234
(Daisy laughs)

00:02:24.234 --> 00:02:25.950
It's a little bit of
settling, but I think...

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:27.210
Is it a tourist thing? I don't know.

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:28.310
I'm fine with average.

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:31.590
- I mean, I've been learning
French for four years.

00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:32.610
- Oh, me too. That's another one.

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:35.491
But that Duolingo owl is
so disappointed in me.

00:02:35.491 --> 00:02:36.324
(Daisy laughs)
Yeah.

00:02:36.324 --> 00:02:38.130
- The Duolingo is thrilled.
- The app changes.

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:40.560
It changes. That owl used to smile at me.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:43.830
And now, I go to the app, he's very angry.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.330
- Duo is very pleased with me,

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:49.200
'cause I'm not joking, I'm on day 1,400.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.491
But I'm like, "Yeah, but
I can't speak French."

00:02:51.491 --> 00:02:52.560
(audience laughs)

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:53.700
I should be fluent.

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:55.653
- You are that committed.
- I am.

00:02:55.653 --> 00:02:58.361
- I can't even get through
the seven day streak.

00:02:58.361 --> 00:03:00.739
(Kelly laughs and claps)

00:03:00.739 --> 00:03:02.940
Literally I get to day six

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:05.100
and there's something
self sabotaging about me

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:06.780
that's just like, "I'm skipping a day."

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:09.720
I'm like, "I don't have to do it."

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:10.740
I'm proud of you right now.

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:11.573
Wow.
- Thank you.

00:03:11.573 --> 00:03:14.040
- You probably know enough
to get by with French.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:14.970
- Yeah.
- Okay.

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:16.470
- And it's the confidence thing, right?

00:03:16.470 --> 00:03:19.560
- Yeah, maybe that's what I'm lacking.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:20.640
You travel so much, you do films.

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:21.960
Are you adventurous when you travel?

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:24.270
- You I've become way less adventurous.

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.220
- I think that's age.
- Yeah.

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:27.090
- So I used to be more
adventurous in my twenties.

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:28.710
Now I'm like, "I might break something."

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:31.950
- Yeah, I mean, I do films
that are quite adventurous.

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:35.310
I recently played the first
woman to swim the Channel.

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:38.070
So I was in the Black Sea
for nine days swimming

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:40.800
and the safety boat would
leave, and then I'm there.

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:42.240
- Alone.
- Alone.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:45.060
And after that I didn't
swim again, and then...

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:46.800
- That's terrifying to me.

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:48.630
That's actually one of those
things that they say...

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:50.130
Your worst fear is just getting left

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:52.170
and just treading water in the ocean.

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:53.790
- And I was like, well,
I knew what was in there

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:55.710
because it was a contained sea.

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:58.230
So I knew the were sharks.
- Oh, then I'd of been fine.

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:01.860
- But my thing is current
and the scary stuff.

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:02.850
But yeah, I've become...

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:06.630
Me and my husband went on a
walk on some famous cliffs.

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:08.160
in Ireland.
- Beautiful.

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:09.420
- I couldn't do it.
- What?

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:10.410
- I was like, (gags).

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:11.998
Literally, (gags).

00:04:11.998 --> 00:04:13.270
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:14.810
So scared.

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:17.520
- Oh my god, it does get very windy too.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:20.520
- It does.
- Yeah, I love that though.

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:23.460
It feels fresh and like a
brand new day. I like it.

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:26.730
Anyway, are you always
affected by heights though?

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:27.900
Are you one of those actors that says

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.640
I can do heights and then you get to it

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:30.473
and then you-
- Yeah.

00:04:30.473 --> 00:04:31.306
- You are, okay?
- Yeah.

00:04:31.306 --> 00:04:33.810
- All of you are the same.
- I'm like the CV liar.

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:36.990
I just did a film where
I play a window cleaner.

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:38.520
And they said...

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:40.110
Oh yeah, this was actually something else

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:41.400
I was supposed to do on a mountain

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:42.360
that I ended up not doing.

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:46.020
So I was learning with an amazing guy.

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:47.580
- You are pretty great.

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:50.378
- That was... Yeah, I was fine.

00:04:50.378 --> 00:04:51.829
(audience applauds)

00:04:51.829 --> 00:04:53.443
- Hurt my knees.

00:04:53.443 --> 00:04:55.113
It hurt my knees watching.

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:58.200
- I was asked if I liked
heights to do this film

00:04:58.200 --> 00:04:59.877
and I was like, "Love heights."

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:01.877
And they were like, "Great.

00:05:01.877 --> 00:05:03.150
We are gonna put you on the side

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:04.560
of a building, yada, yada, yada."

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:05.880
I was like, "Fantastic."

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:07.980
Went home and was like, "Oh
my god, what have I done?"

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:10.800
And then a few weeks later,
we were closer to the film

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:11.970
and they were like, "We're so sorry.

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:13.110
We can't actually put you up.

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:14.160
There's insurance problems."

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:17.580
I was like, "Guys, I was so
looking forward to that."

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:19.537
- The best acting you've
done in the whole film.

00:05:19.537 --> 00:05:22.680
Like, "Oh my god, so sad."

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:25.500
I would never do that
for any amount of money.

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:26.550
I don't mind heights,

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:29.610
but like, why die when
your life is all right?

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:31.985
Why give it the the
chance, you know? Anyway.

00:05:31.985 --> 00:05:32.818
(audience applauds)

00:05:32.818 --> 00:05:35.013
- Her new movie, " Sometimes
I think About Dying."

00:05:35.013 --> 00:05:37.680
It's in theaters now,
very uplifting title.

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:38.613
Explain the movie.

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:41.220
- The film is not sad.

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:42.420
I'm just gonna say that.

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:46.230
The film follows a woman
called Fran, who I play,

00:05:46.230 --> 00:05:48.870
who has some trouble socially,

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:50.040
but has a very original life.

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:52.350
So has these sort of imaginings of death.

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:54.810
Not in a morbid way, just in a,

00:05:54.810 --> 00:05:56.730
that's just what she thinks about.

00:05:56.730 --> 00:06:00.120
And a new guy as played
by Dave, joins the office,

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:01.980
and she is interested in him.

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:05.820
And it's sort of her journey
of overcoming the difficulty

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:07.380
she has in connecting with people.

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:08.310
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:06:08.310 --> 00:06:10.260
I think a lot of people relate to that.

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:12.420
Maybe not think about dying
all the time, but, yeah.

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:14.423
That's a little intense.

00:06:14.423 --> 00:06:18.960
But there's a scene with actual
real bugs crawling on you.

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:20.163
How'd that go over?

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:22.470
- I thought I didn't mind bugs.

00:06:22.470 --> 00:06:24.030
I have one where the ants are crawling

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:25.230
on my hand, that was fine.

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:27.390
And there's one where I
am doing a death Tableau

00:06:27.390 --> 00:06:30.570
and I had some bugs in my
hand, but I couldn't move.

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:32.042
And I was literally like, "Oh, my god."

00:06:32.042 --> 00:06:34.023
I'm just gagging all the time.

00:06:34.857 --> 00:06:37.230
Over the cliff, lying down.
- Everything.

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:39.390
- And that was horrid.

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:41.040
But it's also 'cause you can't move.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:42.600
When you're interacting
with something, it's fine.

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:44.430
- Yeah, but then you feel helpless.

00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:45.630
- Helpless.
- Yeah.

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:47.592
I don't like that.
- No.

00:06:47.592 --> 00:06:49.500
- So there's not a lot of dialogue.

00:06:49.500 --> 00:06:50.610
Do you enjoy that though?

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:52.290
'Cause that's kind of cool as an actor,

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:54.540
just physically in a
different way being able

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:56.160
to interact in a scene.

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:57.540
- Yeah, I feel like I've never done

00:06:57.540 --> 00:07:00.390
the most talky character, to be honest.

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:01.923
But this is my least talky.

00:07:03.390 --> 00:07:05.463
There was the least talking.

00:07:06.456 --> 00:07:08.160
But there was voiceover
the whole way through

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:09.330
and I was like, "Why don't I treat this

00:07:09.330 --> 00:07:10.920
like stage directions instead?"

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:12.510
So in my head I was very busy.

00:07:12.510 --> 00:07:14.130
I learned all the dialogue

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:15.450
so it was like running all the time.

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:18.889
So I felt like I was
speaking, but I wasn't.

00:07:18.889 --> 00:07:21.810
But yeah, I play a quiet person.

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:23.880
- Yeah, you did well with the accent.

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:25.412
- Thank you.

00:07:25.412 --> 00:07:26.245
(audience laughs)

00:07:26.245 --> 00:07:27.563
- You sound amazing.
- Thank you so much.

00:07:29.457 --> 00:07:31.230
- But you also love to sing

00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:33.840
and I hear that you love karaoke, right?

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:35.640
- Yeah.
- What's your go-to?

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:37.680
- Toni Braxton, "Unbreak My Heart."

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:38.638
- Oh, my god.

00:07:38.638 --> 00:07:42.240
(audience applauds and cheers)

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:44.730
You came out with one of the
greatest singers, Toni Braxton,

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:47.310
and then you said the hardest
song, "Unbreak My Heart."

00:07:47.310 --> 00:07:48.630
- I mean, I haven't done
that in a long time,

00:07:48.630 --> 00:07:50.883
but there's a gay bar in Soho.

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:54.000
I mean, they used to have
karaoke every Tuesday.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:55.207
And I remember thinking,

00:07:55.207 --> 00:07:57.390
"I've never felt like
this before in my life."

00:07:57.390 --> 00:07:59.945
I did a song, I was like,
"Everyone's so nice."

00:07:59.945 --> 00:08:01.620
(Kelly laughs)

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:03.360
- I'm incredible?

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:05.490
- I'm amazing, we're all amazing.

00:08:05.490 --> 00:08:06.990
- Everyone's drunk.

00:08:06.990 --> 00:08:09.387
- Exactly, everyone's
like, "What's going on?"

00:08:09.387 --> 00:08:11.100
- I'm just saying "Unbreak
My Heart" is a song

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:13.590
that most people should not attempt.

00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:16.650
That's incredible. You
must be an alto, I'm not.

00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:17.700
- I am an alto, yeah.

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:18.540
Yeah, yeah, yeah,

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:20.190
I mean, I still shouldn't attempt it.

00:08:20.190 --> 00:08:21.210
- No.
- It was just that one time.

00:08:21.210 --> 00:08:24.180
- First of all, at karaoke,
you should attempt everything.

00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:25.530
So I just have to ask,

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:27.060
'cause everybody's a
huge fan of Star Wars,

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:28.110
do you have any kind of tease?

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:30.860
I know you can't say too much, but...

00:08:32.670 --> 00:08:34.443
- It is happening.

00:08:34.443 --> 00:08:36.942
(Kelly laughs)
(audience cheers)

00:08:36.942 --> 00:08:37.775
- Woo!
- Solid news.

00:08:41.034 --> 00:08:42.630
- I know the general story.

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:43.950
Which is very cool.

00:08:43.950 --> 00:08:44.783
- [Kelly] It's been a minute though

00:08:44.783 --> 00:08:46.080
since you've done something.

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:47.820
It's been like, how
long since the last...?

00:08:47.820 --> 00:08:51.150
- Well, what's crazy is time passing.

00:08:51.150 --> 00:08:54.000
It was 11 years ago when I got cast.

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:56.610
- That's right.
- I was a baby.

00:08:56.610 --> 00:08:58.200
- You're still a baby, says your skin.

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:00.343
You're welcome, from genetics.

00:09:00.343 --> 00:09:01.947
(audience laughs)

00:09:01.947 --> 00:09:04.320
- Yeah, so it's been quite a few years

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:06.297
since I've been part of that world.

